IMPORT prelude

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (Western Australia) -- when the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) applies
-- in the State (ss 6, 7 and the compilation table); which local body administers admission and practising certificates under
-- the Law (ss 20-22); applying for and granting admission (ss 113, 114); applying for, renewing and deciding on Australian
-- practising certificates (ss 116-118); and the transitional provisions that carry admission and practice under the Legal
-- Profession Act 2008 (the "old Act") into the Law (ss 262, 276, 278, 279, 289, 322).
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47480, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47480.txt. The deposit names no compilation or reprint number. Its compilation table lists
-- the Act (No. 9 of 2022, assented 14 April 2022; Pt 1 in force 14 April 2022, the rest 1 July 2022 under SL 2022/113 cl 2), the
-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application (Levy) Act 2022, and the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023
-- Pt 15 Div 3 Subdiv 8 (in force 1 July 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0012 (priority 1), raised 3 times by the Western Australian cradle-to-grave life of
-- Daniel (born 1996-04-09): d023 (2019-12-10, aged 23, "Graduates JD; Practical Legal Training"; the scenario notes that in 2020
-- the Legal Profession Act 2008 applied and the event is "replayed under the Uniform Law from 1 July 2022"), d031 (2020-08-24,
-- aged 24, "Admitted by the Supreme Court; a practising certificate"; "Who may engage in legal practice; what is unqualified
-- practice?") and d038 (2029-03-04, aged 32, a conditional costs agreement with a 25% uplift; see lpula-costs.l4). The ledger
-- lists the Uniform Law Part 2.2, the Admission Rules, Uniform Law ss 10, 16-25, 43-49, 181 and 183. Those sections are NOT in
-- this Act: they are in the Legal Profession Uniform Law (Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2014 (Victoria) Schedule 1),
-- applied in WA by s 6 and deposited as a separate subject (legal-profession-uniform-law-wa, ledger au/wa:REQ-0033). SCOPED to what
-- this Act itself says about those questions: whether the Law applied on each event's date, the WA machinery the Law leaves to
-- the State for admission and practising certificates, and the transitional carry-over of a pre-2022 admission and training.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Uniform Law itself (who may practise, s 10; the admission prerequisites, ss 16-25; the grant, conditions and
-- supervised practice of practising certificates, ss 43-49) -- each is an INPUT here where needed; the Admission Rules and the
-- Legal Profession Uniform Regulations (WA) and local regulations (fees, the standard renewal period and the late fee period are
-- INPUTS); Part 3 (the Board and committees), registration certificates (ss 120-122, parallel to ss 116-118), Parts 5 and 7-15,
-- and the transitional provisions other than those named above.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA) -- admission and practising certificates`

§§ `helpers`

-- Dates are written as a single number YYYYMMDD (20 August 2020 is 20200824), so that a later date is a larger number.
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`year of` MEANS FLOOR (`d` DIVIDED BY 10000)

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`month of` MEANS FLOOR ((`d` MODULO 10000) DIVIDED BY 100)

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`day of` MEANS `d` MODULO 100

-- The same day of the month, `n` calendar months later. A day that does not exist in the later month (31 April) is not
-- corrected; the cases avoid such days.
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER, `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months after` MEANS
    FLOOR ((`year of` `d` TIMES 12 PLUS `month of` `d` MINUS 1 PLUS `n`) DIVIDED BY 12) TIMES 10000
    PLUS ((`year of` `d` TIMES 12 PLUS `month of` `d` MINUS 1 PLUS `n`) MODULO 12 PLUS 1) TIMES 100
    PLUS `day of` `d`

§§ `6, 7 and the compilation table -- when the Uniform Law applies in the State`

-- s 6(2): "The Legal Profession Uniform Law -- (a) applies as a law of the State; and (b) as so applying, may be referred to as the
-- Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA); and (c) so applies as if it were an Act."
-- s 7(1): "the Law as in force on 21 June 2021 comes into operation in the State on the day (commencement day) on which this section
-- comes into operation." s 262 defines commencement day for Part 16 the same way.
-- s 2(c): the rest of the Act -- "on a day fixed by proclamation". The compilation table: "Act other than Pt. 1: 1 Jul 2022 (see
-- s. 2(b)(i) and (c) and SL 2022/113 cl. 2)".
-- s 12: if a provision of this Act is inconsistent with the Law, "the provision of this Act prevails".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`commencement day` MEANS 20220701

GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Uniform Law applies in Western Australia on` IF
    `the date` AT LEAST `commencement day`

GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the old Act governs admission and practice on` IF
    `the date` LESS THAN `commencement day`

§§ `20-22 -- designated local authorities`

-- s 20 Table: designated local regulatory authority -- "Section 14: Board"; "Part 2.2: Board"; "Chapter 3, other than section 82(4):
-- Board"; "Section 82(4): Legal Services and Complaints Committee"; "Chapters 4, 5, 6 and 7: Board"; "Section 436(1): Board or Legal
-- Services and Complaints Committee"; and others not encoded.
-- s 21: "the Principal Registrar is the designated local roll authority for the purposes of sections 23, 24 and 462 of the Law."
-- s 22 Table: designated tribunal -- "Sections 23, 100, 101, 119, 120 and 198: State Administrative Tribunal"; "Sections 247 and 248:
-- Supreme Court".
DECLARE `Uniform Law provision` IS ONE OF
    `Part 2.2 (admission)`
    `Chapter 3 (practising certificates), other than s 82(4)`
    `s 82(4)`
    `Chapter 4 (business practice, trust money and costs)`
    `s 436(1)`

DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the Legal Practice Board`
    `the Legal Services and Complaints Committee`
    `the Board or the Legal Services and Complaints Committee`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Uniform Law provision`
GIVETH AN Authority
`the designated local regulatory authority for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `s 82(4)` THEN `the Legal Services and Complaints Committee`
    WHEN `s 436(1)` THEN `the Board or the Legal Services and Complaints Committee`
    OTHERWISE `the Legal Practice Board`

§§ `113, 114 -- admission by the Supreme Court`

-- s 113: "An individual may apply for admission by the Supreme Court under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) section 16 -- (a) in
-- accordance with -- (i) the local regulations; and (ii) the Supreme Court's rules of court; and (iii) a practice direction of the
-- Supreme Court; and (b) by paying the fee (if any) prescribed by the local regulations."
-- Whether the applicant meets the Law's prerequisites (s 17: academic qualifications and practical legal training; suitability)
-- is decided under the Law and is an INPUT here.
DECLARE `Admission application` HAS
    `made in accordance with the local regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in accordance with the rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in accordance with a practice direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a fee is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prescribed fee is paid` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Admission application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the admission application meets s 113` IF
        `the application`'s `made in accordance with the local regulations`
    AND `the application`'s `made in accordance with the rules of court`
    AND `the application`'s `made in accordance with a practice direction`
    AND ((NOT `the application`'s `a fee is prescribed`) OR `the application`'s `the prescribed fee is paid`)

-- s 114: "The Supreme Court must be constituted by at least 3 judges when admitting an individual under the Legal Profession Uniform
-- Law (WA) section 16."
GIVEN `number of judges` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court is properly constituted to admit` IF
    `number of judges` AT LEAST 3

§§ `116 -- applying for an Australian practising certificate`

-- s 116(1): the application "must be -- (a) in the local approved form; and (b) accompanied by the documents or other information
-- required by the local approved form; and (c) accompanied by the fee (if any) prescribed by the local regulations; and (d)
-- accompanied by any annual contribution to the Guarantee Fund required by section 225 of the Law; and (e) accompanied by an amount
-- (if any) required by the local regulations as a contribution towards the cost of funding the State's contribution to the Legal
-- Profession Uniform Framework". The amounts are INPUTS (regulations and the Law).
DECLARE `Certificate application` HAS
    `in the local approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with the documents the form requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with any prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with any Guarantee Fund contribution required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with any framework contribution required` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A `Certificate application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate application meets s 116` IF
        `the application`'s `in the local approved form`
    AND `the application`'s `with the documents the form requires`
    AND `the application`'s `with any prescribed fee`
    AND `the application`'s `with any Guarantee Fund contribution required`
    AND `the application`'s `with any framework contribution required`

§§ `117 -- renewing an Australian practising certificate`

-- s 117(1): a renewal application "must be made within -- (a) the period prescribed by the local regulations as the standard renewal
-- period; or (b) the later period prescribed by the local regulations as the late fee period."
-- (3) the Board "(a) may reject an application for renewal made during the late fee period; and (b) must reject an application for
-- renewal that is not made during the standard renewal period or the late fee period unless the application is accepted under
-- subsection (4)."
-- (4) the Board "may accept an application made within 6 months after the end of the late fee period (even after the expiry of the
-- Australian practising certificate ...)" if satisfied the delay "was caused by matters beyond the control of the applicant" or
-- "there are other circumstances warranting acceptance".
-- The periods are set by regulations and are INPUTS. The late fee period is taken to begin the day after the standard renewal
-- period ends (an inference from "the later period"). An application before the standard renewal period opens is outside both
-- periods and falls to s 117(3)(b); s 117(4) speaks only of applications after the late fee period.
DECLARE `Renewal outcome` IS ONE OF
    `within the standard renewal period`
    `in the late fee period: the Board may reject`
    `late: the Board may accept only if satisfied under s 117(4)`
    `the Board must reject`

GIVEN `lodged on` IS A NUMBER, `standard period opens` IS A NUMBER, `standard period closes` IS A NUMBER, `late fee period closes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Renewal outcome`
`the renewal application is` MEANS
    IF `lodged on` LESS THAN `standard period opens`
    THEN `the Board must reject`
    ELSE IF `lodged on` AT MOST `standard period closes`
         THEN `within the standard renewal period`
         ELSE IF `lodged on` AT MOST `late fee period closes`
              THEN `in the late fee period: the Board may reject`
              ELSE IF `lodged on` AT MOST `months after` `late fee period closes` 6
                   THEN `late: the Board may accept only if satisfied under s 117(4)`
                   ELSE `the Board must reject`

-- s 117(5): if a late application is accepted after expiry, the certificate "(a) is taken to have continued in force on and from the
-- 1 July immediately following its expiry until the Board renews or refuses to renew ... and (b) if renewed, is taken to have been
-- renewed on and from that 1 July."
GIVEN `expired on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 1 July immediately following` MEANS
    IF `expired on` MODULO 10000 LESS THAN 701
    THEN `year of` `expired on` TIMES 10000 PLUS 701
    ELSE (`year of` `expired on` PLUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS 701

§§ `118 -- deemed refusal`

-- s 118(3): "The Board is taken to have refused to grant or renew an Australian practising certificate if the certificate has not
-- been granted, renewed or refused within 6 months after -- (a) if the Board has given the applicant a notice under the Legal
-- Profession Uniform Law (WA) section 95 -- the day specified in the notice by which the applicant was required to comply with
-- the notice; or (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply -- the day on which the application for grant or renewal was lodged."
GIVEN `lodged on` IS A NUMBER, `a s 95 notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the s 95 compliance day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deemed refusal runs from` MEANS
    IF `a s 95 notice was given` THEN `the s 95 compliance day` ELSE `lodged on`

GIVEN `lodged on` IS A NUMBER, `a s 95 notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the s 95 compliance day` IS A NUMBER, `decided` IS A BOOLEAN, `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is taken to have refused` IF
        (NOT `decided`)
    AND `today` GREATER THAN `months after` (`the deemed refusal runs from` `lodged on` `a s 95 notice was given` `the s 95 compliance day`) 6

§§ `276, 278, 279 -- admission begun under the old Act`

-- s 276: if a person applied to the full bench "under section 25(1) of the old Act" and "the application was not decided under the old
-- Act before commencement day", it is "taken, on and from commencement day, to be an application under section 113".
GIVEN `applied under old Act s 25(1) on` IS A NUMBER, `decided before commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the old application continues as a s 113 application` IF
        `applied under old Act s 25(1) on` LESS THAN `commencement day`
    AND (NOT `decided before commencement day`)

-- s 278: a person who "obtained approved academic qualifications or corresponding academic qualifications (as those terms were defined
-- in section 21(1) of the old Act) before commencement day ... is taken, on and from commencement day, to have attained the academic
-- qualifications referred to in the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) section 17(1)(a)."
GIVEN `qualifications obtained on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the old academic qualifications count under Uniform Law s 17(1)(a)` IF
    `qualifications obtained on` LESS THAN `commencement day`

-- s 279(2): PLT requirements "satisfactorily completed ... before commencement day" count for Law s 17(1)(b).
-- (3), (4): if "partially completed ... before commencement day" and completed "within the period of 12 months beginning on commencement
-- day", the person is taken, "from when the person completes the requirements", to have completed the Law's requirements.
-- A person who began after commencement day is outside s 279; the Law and the Admission Rules govern (FALSE here means only that
-- s 279 does not carry the training over).
GIVEN `began PLT before commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN, `completed PLT on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 279 carries the old PLT into Uniform Law s 17(1)(b)` IF
        `began PLT before commencement day`
    AND `completed PLT on` LESS THAN `months after` `commencement day` 12

§§ `289, 322 -- practice and the roll carried over`

-- s 322: "The roll of persons admitted to the legal profession maintained by the Supreme Court under section 28(1) of the old Act
-- continues on and from commencement day as the Supreme Court roll under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) section 22(1)."
-- The Act carries the ROLL over; it has no section deeming an old-Act admission to be an admission under the Law. That a person on
-- the old roll is, after commencement day, an Australian lawyer on the Supreme Court roll is an inference from s 322 (and the Law's
-- Schedule 4, clauses 11 to 18 of which s 266(2) applies; not deposited here).
GIVEN `admitted under the old Act on` IS A NUMBER, `removed from the roll before commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name continues on the Supreme Court roll` IF
        `admitted under the old Act on` LESS THAN `commencement day`
    AND (NOT `removed from the roll before commencement day`)

-- s 289(1): "A person who engaged in a period of supervised legal practice (as defined in section 3 of the old Act) before commencement
-- day is taken, on and from commencement day, to have completed the same period of supervised legal practice for the purposes of the
-- Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) section 49(1)."
-- (2): the whole required period is taken to be completed if the person "(a) had the required experience (as defined in section 50(1)
-- of the old Act); or (b) was entitled to practise on their own account under the Legal Practitioners Act 1893 or the Legal Practice
-- Act 2003." The length of the period the Law requires is in s 49 of the Law, not here; it is an INPUT.
GIVEN `supervised practice began on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 289 counts the period before commencement day` IF
    `supervised practice began on` LESS THAN `commencement day`

GIVEN `had the old Act s 50(1) required experience` IS A BOOLEAN, `entitled to practise on own account under the 1893 or 2003 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 289 treats the whole supervised period as completed` IF
        `had the old Act s 50(1) required experience`
    OR  `entitled to practise on own account under the 1893 or 2003 Act`
